%section.hero
  .container.hero__grid
    .hero__text
      %h1 Cut Rubies with ease!
      %p.lead
        Ruby Version Manager (RVM) is a command-line tool to install, manage, and work with
        multiple ruby environments, from interpreters to sets of gems.
      .hero__actions
        %a.key.key--primary{ href: "/rvm/install/" } Installation guide
        %a.textlink{ href: "#docindex" } Browse the documentation
    .install.graphite
      %ol.install__steps
        %li
          %h2.install__title Install GPG keys
          = sh_cmd "gpg2 --keyserver keyserver.ubuntu.com --recv-keys 409B6B1796C275462A1703113804BB82D39DC0E3 7D2BAF1CF37B13E2069D6956105BD0E739499BDB"
        %li
          %h2.install__title Install RVM
          = sh_cmd "\\curl -sSL https://get.rvm.io | bash -s stable"
        %li
          %h2.install__title Or with default Ruby and Rails in one command
          = sh_cmd "\\curl -sSL https://get.rvm.io | bash -s stable --rails"
      %p.install__note
        In case you encounter an issues or want to know more, check
        %a{ href: "/rvm/security/" } security.

